IMPORT prelude

-- Aged Care Act 2024 (Cth) -- what an older person seeking care meets: who can apply and be found eligible for an aged care
-- needs assessment (ss 7 "care needs", 56, 58, 61(2), 62(3)(c)); what can be approved, and whether it is home support (Support
-- at Home) or residential care (ss 8(3), 10, 65(2)-(3), 66-68); the priority category and the place (ss 84(1)-(2), 86(5),
-- 92(1A)); whether I can get funded home support services now (s 9(2)); an approval reaching back to my first service day
-- (s 71(2)-(4)); revoking on request (ss 72, 73(1)); the notices I must be given and by when (ss 59, 64(3), 70, 73(2), 79, 88,
-- 280(6), 314(2), 314A(5), 320(5)); what I contribute at home (s 273) and in a residential care home (ss 276-279, 280(1),
-- 281, 282, 296, 298, 301, 305, 319); and the Statement of Rights, its effect and where to complain (ss 23, 24, 358(a)).
--
-- SEAT: the older person seeking care -- "Am I eligible for Support at Home, and what do I contribute?". Every decision is
-- phrased as that person asks it. Where the Act addresses the System Governor ("must not make an eligibility determination
-- ... unless"), it is encoded as what can be decided for me; where it addresses the registered provider ("must not accept",
-- "may charge"), as what I can be asked to pay. Where the Act hands a judgment to the System Governor or the needs assessor
-- (ss 61(2)(b), 65(1), 71(4)), it is asked as a fact: "if the System Governor is satisfied that ...".
--
-- Provisions covered: ss 7 ("care needs", "lifetime cap", "start day"), 8(3), 9(2)(a)-(e), 10(1), (2), (4), (6), (7), 56(1),
-- 58, 59(1), 61(2), 62(3)(c), 64(3), 65(1)-(3), 66, 67(1)-(3), 68, 70(1), 71(2)-(4), 72, 73(1), (2), 79(1), 84(1), (2),
-- 86(5), 88(1), 92(1A), 92A(1), (2), 244(7), 273(1)-(3), (5), 276(1), (2)(a), 277(1)-(3), 278, 279(1)-(5), 280(1), (6),
-- 281(3), (4), 282(2), 296(a), 298(a)-(c), 301, 305, 314(2), 314A(5), 319(1)-(3), 320(5), 23, 24(1), (3), 358(a)(ii).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 2, compilation date 1 July 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 45, 2025), register id
-- C2026C00301, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2024A00104.txt. The Aged Care Rules 2025 set most of the numbers
-- this Act points to (the individual contribution rates, the lifetime cap, the income and asset thresholds, the maximum
-- accommodation and hotelling supplement amounts, the maximum non-clinical care contribution, the basic daily fee, prescribed
-- periods); they are NOT deposited, so every one of them is an INPUT here, and no figure from them is stated as fact.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. The supporter regime (Part 4 of Chapter 1); classification assessments, levels and reassessments (Part 3 of
-- Chapter 2) beyond whether a classification decision is in effect; reassessment (s 64) beyond its notice; the place numbers
-- and allocation method (ss 91, 93) and places allocated to providers under specialist aged care programs (ss 94-102);
-- specialist aged care programs throughout (ss 247-250, 272, 275, 286); assistive technology and home modifications beyond
-- the priority-category question and the s 273 Step 1 rate; how the System Governor fixes my individual contribution rate
-- (s 314(1): "in accordance with any criteria or methods prescribed by the rules" -- the rate is an INPUT); total assessable
-- income and the value of assets (ss 322-335 -- INPUTS); the compensation payment fee (ss 274, 277(3) -- an INPUT); the
-- fee reduction supplement (an INPUT); the s 277(4) reductions under rules for s 231(3); means not disclosed status at home
-- beyond its notice (s 314A); short-term residential care (respite, s 283), higher everyday living fees (s 284), prescribed
-- classes (Division 2A); accommodation agreements, refundable deposit balances, deductions and refunds (ss 289-295, 303-313)
-- beyond s 305; the subsidies themselves (Chapter 4 Parts 2-3: what the Commonwealth pays the provider); the provider
-- obligations, regulation, complaints process, review of decisions, information and penalties (Chapters 3, 5-8). Borrowed
-- terms -- "Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person", "homeless", "sickness", "impairment", "basic age pension amount"
-- (Social Security Act 1991 point 1064-B1) -- are asked as facts. Machinery (the Commission, the Advisory Council, rule-making
-- power, commencement) is out.
--
-- Money is in dollars; percentages are written as numbers (50 means 50%). Periods are counted in days.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Aged Care Act 2024`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER
      `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER
      `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

-- "rounding down to the nearest cent" (ss 277(2)(b), 281(4)(b)). Every amount here is positive, so truncation is rounding down.
GIVEN `amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded down to the cent` MEANS
    TRUNC `amount` 2

§§ `s 7 -- care needs`

-- s 7: "care needs means one or both of the following that apply in relation to an individual: (a) the individual has
-- difficulty (whether physical, mental or social) undertaking any daily living activities; (b) the individual requires help
-- from another person, or the assistance of one or more aids, to maintain their physical, mental or social capacity to function
-- independently." Gloss: care needs are what the needs assessment is about; s 58(b) asks only that information about them be
-- given, not that they be proved.
@export Do I have care needs as the Act defines them (s 7)?
GIVEN `I have difficulty with daily living activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have difficulty (physical, mental or social) with any daily living activities
      `I need help or aids to keep functioning independently` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you need another person's help, or aids, to maintain your capacity to function independently
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I have care needs` IF
        `I have difficulty with daily living activities`
    OR  `I need help or aids to keep functioning independently`

§§ `ss 56, 58 -- applying, and being found eligible for an aged care needs assessment`

-- s 56(1): "An individual, or a person in a class of persons prescribed by the rules on behalf of the individual, may apply, in an
-- approved form, to the System Governor for access to funded aged care services if the individual does not have an eligibility
-- determination for an aged care needs assessment that is in effect." Gloss: the System Governor is the Secretary of the
-- Department (s 6 outline).
@export May I apply for access to funded aged care services (s 56(1))?
GIVEN `an eligibility determination is in effect for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you already have an eligibility determination for an aged care needs assessment in effect
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply for access to funded aged care services` IF
    (NOT `an eligibility determination is in effect for me`)

-- s 58(a): "the individual: (i) is aged 65 or over; or (ii) is an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person and is aged at
-- least 50; or (iii) is homeless, or at risk of homelessness, and is aged at least 50".
@export Am I old enough to be assessed for aged care (s 58(a))?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `I am an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person
      `I am homeless or at risk of homelessness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are homeless, or at risk of homelessness
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I old enough to be assessed for aged care` IF
        `my age` AT LEAST 65
    OR  (`I am an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person` AND `my age` AT LEAST 50)
    OR  (`I am homeless or at risk of homelessness` AND `my age` AT LEAST 50)

-- s 58: "The System Governor must not make an eligibility determination for an aged care needs assessment for an individual
-- unless the System Governor considers that: (a) [age, above]; and (b) information of a kind prescribed by the rules has been
-- provided relating to the individual's care needs; and (c) if the individual is aged less than 65, the individual: (i) has
-- elected, in the approved form, to be provided with funded aged care services before the individual turns 65; and (ii) has been
-- informed of any other services that may be available to meet the care needs of the individual." s 58 is a bar, not a grant:
-- when every limb holds the System Governor may make the determination; s 57(1) says only that it "must ... decide whether".
@export Can I be found eligible for an aged care needs assessment (s 58)?
GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years
      `I am an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person
      `I am homeless or at risk of homelessness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are homeless, or at risk of homelessness
      `the information the rules ask for about my care needs has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the information the Aged Care Rules prescribe about your care needs has been provided
      `I have elected to get funded aged care before turning 65` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have elected, in the approved form, to be provided with funded aged care services before you turn 65
      `I have been told of other services that may meet my care needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have been informed of any other services that may meet your care needs
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be found eligible for an aged care needs assessment` IF
        `Am I old enough to be assessed for aged care` `my age` `I am an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person` `I am homeless or at risk of homelessness`
    AND `the information the rules ask for about my care needs has been given`
    AND (    `my age` AT LEAST 65
         OR  (    `I have elected to get funded aged care before turning 65`
              AND `I have been told of other services that may meet my care needs`))

-- s 61(2): "the aged care needs assessment must not be undertaken, and the individual's application ... is taken to be
-- withdrawn, if: (a) an eligibility determination for an aged care needs assessment is not in effect for the individual; or (b)
-- the System Governor is satisfied it is not reasonably possible for an approved needs assessor to undertake the assessment."
-- Note to s 61(2): an example is "where the individual does not provide consent to the assessment".
@export Will my aged care needs assessment go ahead (s 61(2))?
GIVEN `an eligibility determination is in effect for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an eligibility determination for an aged care needs assessment is in effect for you
      `the System Governor is satisfied an assessment is not reasonably possible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the System Governor is satisfied an approved needs assessor cannot reasonably assess you (for example, you do not consent)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my aged care needs assessment go ahead` IF
        `an eligibility determination is in effect for me`
    AND (NOT `the System Governor is satisfied an assessment is not reasonably possible`)

-- s 62(3): the approved needs assessor must "(c) involve the individual's carer, family member, advocate or other person in the
-- discussions mentioned in subsection (2), if that is the individual's will and preference."
@export Must the assessor bring my carer or family into the assessment discussions (s 62(3)(c))?
GIVEN `I want my carer, family or advocate involved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is your will and preference that your carer, family member, advocate or other person be involved
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the assessor bring my carer or family into the discussions` IF
    `I want my carer, family or advocate involved`

§§ `ss 8(3), 10 -- Support at Home or residential care: where the care is delivered`

-- s 8(3): "a service group means any of the following: (a) home support; (b) residential care; (c) assistive technology; (d) home
-- modifications." Gloss: "Support at Home" is the program name for home support; the Act never uses that name.
DECLARE `Service group` IS ONE OF
    `home support`
    `residential care`
    `assistive technology`
    `home modifications`

-- s 7 "classification type": "(a) ongoing; (b) short-term; (c) hospital transition."
DECLARE `Classification type` IS ONE OF
    `ongoing`
    `short-term`
    `hospital transition`

-- s 10(4), (7): places named as not a residential care home, or not a home or community setting.
DECLARE `Where I live or would get care` IS ONE OF
    `my own home`
    `a retirement village`
    `a place in the community`
    `an approved residential care home`
    `an NDIS-funded group home`
    `a hospital`
    `a psychiatric facility`
    `a prison or detention centre`
    `a hospice or palliative care facility`

-- s 10(6): "A home or community setting means a place in a home, or in the community, where funded aged care services are
-- delivered." (7): "does not include ... (a) a group home funded under the National Disability Insurance Scheme; (b) a hospital;
-- (c) a psychiatric facility; (d) a prison or detention centre; (e) a hospice or facility that primarily provides palliative care;
-- (f) any other place prescribed by the rules." INFERENCE: an approved residential care home is treated as not a home or
-- community setting, because s 10(1) offers the two settings as alternatives ("(a) an approved residential care home; or (b) a
-- home or community setting") and s 8(1)(e), (f) assigns each its own service groups; s 10(7) does not itself list it.
@export Can home support be delivered to me where I am (s 10(6), (7))?
GIVEN `the place` IS A `Where I live or would get care` @desc Where you live, or would receive the care
      `the rules exclude the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Aged Care Rules prescribe the place as not a home or community setting (s 10(7)(f))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the place a home or community setting` IF
    (NOT `the rules exclude the place`)
    AND (CONSIDER `the place`
         WHEN `my own home` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a retirement village` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `a place in the community` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)

-- s 8(1)(e), (f): the rules must "specify, for the service groups home support, assistive technology and home modifications,
-- that all service types in those service groups must be delivered in a home or community setting" and "for the service group
-- residential care, that all service types in the service group must be delivered in a residential care home". s 10(4)(a), (b):
-- a residential care home "does not include ... (a) a private home; (b) a retirement village (other than a place referred to in
-- paragraph (3)(b))".
DECLARE `The care I can get where I am` IS ONE OF
    `home support, assistive technology or home modifications`
    `residential care`
    `no funded aged care service group`

@export Which kind of funded aged care can be delivered where I am, Support at Home or residential care (ss 8(1)(e), (f), 10)?
GIVEN `the place` IS A `Where I live or would get care` @desc Where you live, or would receive the care
      `the rules exclude the place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Aged Care Rules prescribe the place as not a home or community setting (s 10(7)(f))
GIVETH A `The care I can get where I am`
`Which kind of care can be delivered where I am` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the place` EQUALS `an approved residential care home` THEN `residential care`
        IF `Is the place a home or community setting` `the place` `the rules exclude the place`
           THEN `home support, assistive technology or home modifications`
        OTHERWISE `no funded aged care service group`

§§ `ss 65-68 -- what can be approved for me`

-- s 65(1): the System Governor must "decide whether or not the individual requires access to funded aged care services". (3):
-- "the System Governor must not approve a service group, service type or funded aged care service under subsection (2) for an
-- individual unless: (a) section 66, 67 or 68 applies in relation to the individual and the service group, service type or
-- service; and (b) any eligibility requirements prescribed by the rules for the service group ... are met." s 66: "This section
-- applies in relation to an individual and any service group if the individual is an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander
-- person." s 67(1): "(a) the individual has a long-term physical, mental, sensory or intellectual impairment and the impairment
-- may hinder the individual's participation in society on an equal basis with others ...; and (b) any of the following apply:
-- (i)-(vii)" [community living and inclusion; personal mobility; mobility aids or assistive technology; a health service needed
-- because of the impairment; habilitation or rehabilitation; help to reach those; preventing a further impairment]. (2): "a
-- medical service required by the individual because of sickness". (3): s 67 applies to home support "only to the extent to
-- which this section applies to the service types or funded aged care services in the service group".
@export Can home support services of this type be approved for me (ss 65(1), (3), 66, 67)?
GIVEN `the System Governor decides I require access to funded aged care services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the System Governor, on your assessment report, decides you require access (s 65(1))
      `I am an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person
      `I have a long-term impairment that may hinder my equal participation in society` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have a long-term physical, mental, sensory or intellectual impairment that may hinder your participation on an equal basis (s 67(1)(a))
      `the service type meets a purpose in s 67(1)(b) for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the services meet one of the purposes in s 67(1)(b)(i)-(vii) for you
      `the service type is a medical service I need because of sickness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the services are a medical service you need because of sickness (s 67(2))
      `the rules' eligibility requirements for home support are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any eligibility requirements in the Aged Care Rules for home support are met
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can home support services of this type be approved for me` IF
        `the System Governor decides I require access to funded aged care services`
    AND `the rules' eligibility requirements for home support are met`
    AND (    `I am an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person`
         OR  (    `I have a long-term impairment that may hinder my equal participation in society`
              AND `the service type meets a purpose in s 67(1)(b) for me`)
         OR  `the service type is a medical service I need because of sickness`)

-- s 68: "This section applies in relation to an individual and the residential care service group if the individual has, by
-- reason of sickness, a continuing need for funded aged care services (including nursing services) in the service group." s 67
-- does not reach residential care (s 67(3) names only home support, assistive technology and home modifications).
@export Can residential care be approved for me (ss 65(1), (3), 66, 68)?
GIVEN `the System Governor decides I require access to funded aged care services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the System Governor, on your assessment report, decides you require access (s 65(1))
      `I am an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person
      `I have a continuing need for care including nursing because of sickness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, because of sickness, you have a continuing need for residential care services, including nursing
      `the rules' eligibility requirements for residential care are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any eligibility requirements in the Aged Care Rules for residential care are met
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can residential care be approved for me` IF
        `the System Governor decides I require access to funded aged care services`
    AND `the rules' eligibility requirements for residential care are met`
    AND (    `I am an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person`
         OR  `I have a continuing need for care including nursing because of sickness`)

-- s 65(2)(b): "if the service group is home support, assistive technology or home modifications and the individual is not an
-- Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person: (i) whether to approve one or more service types in that group for the individual".
-- Gloss: for everyone else, a home support approval names the service types; an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person's
-- approval covers the whole group.
@export Will my approval be limited to particular service types (s 65(2)(b))?
GIVEN `the service group` IS A `Service group` @desc The service group approved
      `I am an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will my approval be limited to particular service types` IF
        (NOT `I am an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person`)
    AND (NOT (`the service group` EQUALS `residential care`))

§§ `ss 84, 86(5) -- priority categories`

-- s 84(1)(b): a prioritisation assessment is undertaken for "(i) ongoing for home support; or (ii) ongoing or short-term for
-- assistive technology; or (iii) short-term for home modifications; or (iv) ongoing for residential care". (2): not required
-- for ongoing home support if "the circumstances prescribed by the rules apply".
@export Must I be given a priority category before I can be allocated a place (s 84)?
GIVEN `the service group` IS A `Service group` @desc The service group
      `the classification type` IS A `Classification type` @desc Ongoing, short-term or hospital transition
      `the rules excuse me from prioritisation for ongoing home support` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether circumstances in the Aged Care Rules apply so that no prioritisation is needed for ongoing home support (s 84(2))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be given a priority category` IF
    CONSIDER `the service group`
    WHEN `home support` THEN (`the classification type` EQUALS `ongoing`) AND (NOT `the rules excuse me from prioritisation for ongoing home support`)
    WHEN `assistive technology` THEN (`the classification type` EQUALS `ongoing`) OR (`the classification type` EQUALS `short-term`)
    WHEN `home modifications` THEN `the classification type` EQUALS `short-term`
    WHEN `residential care` THEN `the classification type` EQUALS `ongoing`

-- s 86(5): for ongoing residential care the System Governor must "(a) assign the individual priority category 1 if: (i) the
-- individual has an urgency rating of high; or (ii) the individual resides in an area prescribed by the rules; or (iii) the
-- individual is an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person, homeless, or in a class of persons prescribed by the rules; or (b)
-- ... priority category 2 if ... the individual has an urgency rating of medium; or (c) ... priority category 3 if ... low."
DECLARE `Urgency rating` IS ONE OF
    `high`
    `medium`
    `low`

@export What priority category must I be given for permanent residential care (s 86(5))?
GIVEN `my urgency rating` IS A `Urgency rating` @desc The urgency rating from your prioritisation assessment
      `I live in an area the rules prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you reside in an area prescribed by the Aged Care Rules
      `I am Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander, homeless, or in a prescribed class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person, homeless, or in a class prescribed by the rules
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What priority category must I be given for residential care` MEANS
    IF `I live in an area the rules prescribe` OR `I am Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander, homeless, or in a prescribed class`
    THEN 1
    ELSE CONSIDER `my urgency rating`
         WHEN `high` THEN 1
         WHEN `medium` THEN 2
         WHEN `low` THEN 3

§§ `s 9(2) -- can I get funded home support services now`

-- s 9(2): "An individual can access a funded aged care service through a service group if: (a) the individual makes an
-- application ... under section 56; and (b) the System Governor makes an eligibility determination for the individual and that
-- determination is in effect; and (c) the individual undergoes an aged care needs assessment; and (d) an access approval that
-- covers the service is in effect for the individual; and (e) if the individual is accessing the service other than under a
-- specialist aged care program: (i) a classification decision establishing a classification level in a classification type for
-- the service group is in effect for the individual; and (ii) if a priority category decision is required under section 86 ...
-- such a decision under section 86 has been made ...; and (iii) if the classification type or classification level is one for
-- which the System Governor may allocate the individual a place under section 92--a place has been allocated to the individual
-- under that section ... and is in effect." s 92(1A): no allocation under s 92(1) for ongoing home support if "the
-- circumstances prescribed by the rules apply". s 92A(1): a home support place "takes effect on the start day for the individual
-- included in a start notification given by a registered provider"; (2): if that start day "is not within the period prescribed
-- by the rules, the place: (a) does not take effect; and (b) is taken to be withdrawn". Specialist aged care programs (s 9(2)(f))
-- are not encoded.
DECLARE `My path into ongoing home support`
    HAS `I have applied for access` IS A BOOLEAN
        `an eligibility determination is in effect for me` IS A BOOLEAN
        `I have undergone an aged care needs assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
        `an access approval covering the service is in effect for me` IS A BOOLEAN
        `a classification decision for ongoing home support is in effect for me` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the rules excuse me from prioritisation for ongoing home support` IS A BOOLEAN
        `a priority category decision has been made for me` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the rules excuse me from a place allocation for ongoing home support` IS A BOOLEAN
        `a place has been allocated to me` IS A BOOLEAN
        `a provider's start notification names a start day for me` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the start day is within the period the rules prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `What I am still waiting for` IS ONE OF
    `nothing -- I can get the service`
    `to apply`
    `an eligibility determination`
    `an aged care needs assessment`
    `an access approval covering the service`
    `a classification decision`
    `a priority category decision`
    `a place to be allocated`
    `a provider to start my services within the period the rules allow`

@export What am I still waiting for before I can get funded home support services (ss 9(2), 92(1A), 92A)?
GIVEN `my path` IS A `My path into ongoing home support` @desc Where you are on the way into ongoing home support
GIVETH A `What I am still waiting for`
`What am I still waiting for` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `my path`'s `I have applied for access`) THEN `to apply`
        IF (NOT `my path`'s `an eligibility determination is in effect for me`) THEN `an eligibility determination`
        IF (NOT `my path`'s `I have undergone an aged care needs assessment`) THEN `an aged care needs assessment`
        IF (NOT `my path`'s `an access approval covering the service is in effect for me`) THEN `an access approval covering the service`
        IF (NOT `my path`'s `a classification decision for ongoing home support is in effect for me`) THEN `a classification decision`
        IF (NOT `my path`'s `the rules excuse me from prioritisation for ongoing home support`)
           AND (NOT `my path`'s `a priority category decision has been made for me`)
           THEN `a priority category decision`
        IF `my path`'s `the rules excuse me from a place allocation for ongoing home support` THEN `nothing -- I can get the service`
        IF (NOT `my path`'s `a place has been allocated to me`) THEN `a place to be allocated`
        IF (NOT `my path`'s `a provider's start notification names a start day for me`)
           OR (NOT `my path`'s `the start day is within the period the rules prescribe`)
           THEN `a provider to start my services within the period the rules allow`
        OTHERWISE `nothing -- I can get the service`

@export Can I get funded home support services now (s 9(2))?
GIVEN `my path` IS A `My path into ongoing home support` @desc Where you are on the way into ongoing home support
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I get funded home support services now` IF
    `What am I still waiting for` `my path` EQUALS `nothing -- I can get the service`

§§ `s 71(2)-(4) -- an approval reaching back to my first service day`

-- s 71(2): the access approval may take effect on a day "earlier than the day the access approval is given if: (a) the
-- individual makes an application, in the approved form, within the period referred to in subsection (3); and (b) the System
-- Governor is satisfied that any of the circumstances set out in subsection (4) apply ...; and (c) the day is no earlier than the
-- first day a funded aged care service was delivered to the individual." (3): "(a) the period of 5 days after the first day an
-- aged care service covered by the approval was delivered to the individual; or (b) if circumstances prescribed by the rules
-- apply--the period prescribed by the rules; or (c) if the System Governor determines a period for the individual under
-- subsection (6)--that period." (4): "(a) the individual urgently needed access ... and there was a significant risk of harm ...;
-- or (b) the individual is an Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander person and ... there was a lack of availability of an approved
-- needs assessor to undertake a culturally safe aged care needs assessment ...; or (c) the individual commenced accessing funded
-- aged care services under a specialist aged care program ... and ... there was a significant delay in the availability of an
-- approved needs assessor".
@export Can my access approval start from the day my services first began (s 71(2)-(4))?
GIVEN `days after my first service that I applied` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the first day a covered service was delivered you made the application
      `the period that applies to me in days` IS A NUMBER @desc 5, unless the Aged Care Rules prescribe a period or the System Governor determined a longer one for you (s 71(3))
      `the System Governor is satisfied a s 71(4) circumstance applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the System Governor is satisfied you urgently needed care at significant risk of harm, or a s 71(4)(b) or (c) circumstance applied
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my access approval start from my first service day` IF
        `days after my first service that I applied` AT MOST `the period that applies to me in days`
    AND `the System Governor is satisfied a s 71(4) circumstance applies`

§§ `ss 72, 73 -- giving up an eligibility determination or an approval`

-- s 72(1): "An individual may request the System Governor revoke an eligibility determination ... if the individual is under age
-- 65 at the time of making the request." (2): "If an access approval is in effect for an individual, the individual may request
-- the System Governor to revoke the approval." s 73(1): "the System Governor must revoke ... within 28 days after the day the
-- request is made."
DECLARE `What I want revoked` IS ONE OF
    `my eligibility determination`
    `my access approval`

@export May I ask for it to be revoked (s 72)?
GIVEN `what` IS A `What I want revoked` @desc The eligibility determination or the access approval
      `my age` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age when you make the request
      `it is in effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the determination or approval is in effect for you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I ask for it to be revoked` IF
    `it is in effect`
    AND (CONSIDER `what`
         WHEN `my eligibility determination` THEN `my age` LESS THAN 65
         WHEN `my access approval` THEN TRUE)

@export Within how many days of my request must it be revoked (s 73(1))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Within how many days must my revocation request be granted` MEANS 28

§§ `notices -- what I must be told, and by when`

-- s 59(1): notice of a decision not to make an eligibility determination "within 14 days after the day the decision is made";
-- s 64(3): that no reassessment is required, "within 14 days after the decision is made"; s 70(1): "written notice of a decision
-- under subsection 65(1) or (2) ... within 14 days after the decision is made"; s 73(2): of a revocation on request, "within 14
-- days after making the decision"; s 79(1): a classification decision, "within 14 days after the decision is made"; s 88(1): a
-- priority category decision, "within 14 days"; s 314(2): the individual contribution rate, "within 14 days after the
-- determination is made"; ss 314A(5), 320(5): means not disclosed status, "Within 14 days after making a determination"; s
-- 280(6)(a): a decision on whether my residential hotelling and non-clinical care contributions are to be taken as zero, "28
-- days after the application was made" (or after further information requested is received).
DECLARE `The decision I am waiting to hear about` IS ONE OF
    `a refusal to make me eligible for a needs assessment`
    `a decision that no reassessment is required`
    `my access approval decision`
    `a revocation I asked for`
    `my classification decision`
    `my priority category decision`
    `my individual contribution rate`
    `a decision that I have means not disclosed status`
    `my application to have my residential contributions taken as zero`

@export Within how many days must I be given written notice of the decision (ss 59, 64, 70, 73, 79, 88, 280, 314, 314A, 320)?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision I am waiting to hear about` @desc The decision
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Within how many days must I be told` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `my application to have my residential contributions taken as zero` THEN 28
    OTHERWISE 14

§§ `s 273 -- what I contribute for Support at Home`

-- s 273(1): a registered provider delivering a service "through the service group home support, assistive technology or home
-- modifications to an individual on a day may charge the individual an individual contribution for that service." (2) Method
-- statement: "Step 1. Work out: (a) if the service group is home support--the individual's individual contribution rate under
-- section 314 ...; (b) if the service group is assistive technology or home modifications--the lower of the individual's
-- individual contribution rate under section 314 for the day ... and the day prescribed by the rules. Step 2. If the subsidy
-- basis for the service is efficient price or unit price--multiply the number of hours or units of the service delivered ... by
-- the lesser of the following: (a) the base efficient price or base unit price for the service on that day; (b) the price charged
-- by the provider for an hour or unit of the service on that day. Step 3. Multiply the Step 1 amount: (a) if the subsidy basis
-- ... is efficient price or unit price--by the Step 2 amount; or (b) if the subsidy basis ... is cost and circumstances prescribed
-- by the rules apply--by the amount prescribed by the rules ...; or (c) if the subsidy basis ... is cost and paragraph (b) does not
-- apply--by the cost. Step 4. Reduce (but not below zero) the Step 3 amount by any fee reduction supplement applicable to the
-- individual for the day." Gloss: the individual contribution rate is a percentage for each "means testing category" --
-- clinical supports, independence, everyday living (s 8(4)) -- fixed for me by the System Governor under rules not deposited.
DECLARE `Subsidy basis` IS ONE OF
    `efficient price or unit price`
    `cost`

DECLARE `The service on the day`
    HAS `my contribution rate for its means testing category` IS A NUMBER
        `my rate on the day the rules prescribe` IS A NUMBER
        `its subsidy basis` IS A `Subsidy basis`
        `hours or units delivered` IS A NUMBER
        `base efficient or unit price` IS A NUMBER
        `the provider's price per hour or unit` IS A NUMBER
        `its cost, or the rules' amount for it` IS A NUMBER
        `my fee reduction supplement for the day` IS A NUMBER

-- s 273(5): "the individual contribution ... is zero if, on a previous day (the trigger day), the total of the following exceeds
-- the lifetime cap on the trigger day: (a) the sum of any individual contributions charged to the individual under this section
-- for the delivery of other funded aged care services; (b) the sum of any non-clinical care contributions charged to the
-- individual under section 279; (c) any other contribution or fee prescribed by the rules." s 279(5) says the same of the
-- non-clinical care contribution. s 7: "lifetime cap means the amount prescribed by the rules" (an INPUT).
@export Has the lifetime cap ended what I contribute (ss 273(5), 279(5))?
GIVEN `individual contributions charged to me before today` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the s 273 individual contributions charged to you up to the end of an earlier day
      `non-clinical care contributions charged to me before today` IS A NUMBER @desc The sum of the s 279 non-clinical care contributions charged to you up to the end of that day
      `other contributions the rules count` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other contributions or fees the rules count toward the cap
      `the lifetime cap` IS A NUMBER @desc The lifetime cap prescribed by the Aged Care Rules on that day
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Has the lifetime cap ended what I contribute` IF
    (`individual contributions charged to me before today` PLUS `non-clinical care contributions charged to me before today` PLUS `other contributions the rules count`)
        GREATER THAN `the lifetime cap`

@export How much can I be charged as my individual contribution for a home care service on a day (s 273(2), (5))?
GIVEN `the service group` IS A `Service group` @desc Home support, assistive technology or home modifications
      `the service` IS A `The service on the day` @desc The service delivered and its prices
      `the lifetime cap has been passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on an earlier day, your counted contributions exceeded the lifetime cap (s 273(5))
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my individual contribution for the service` MEANS
    IF `the lifetime cap has been passed` OR `the service group` EQUALS `residential care`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the greater of` 0 (`step 3` MINUS `the service`'s `my fee reduction supplement for the day`)
    WHERE
        `step 1` MEANS
            IF `the service group` EQUALS `home support`
            THEN `the service`'s `my contribution rate for its means testing category`
            ELSE `the lesser of` (`the service`'s `my contribution rate for its means testing category`) (`the service`'s `my rate on the day the rules prescribe`)
        `step 2` MEANS
            `the service`'s `hours or units delivered`
                TIMES (`the lesser of` (`the service`'s `base efficient or unit price`) (`the service`'s `the provider's price per hour or unit`))
        `step 3` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the service`'s `its subsidy basis`
            WHEN `efficient price or unit price` THEN (`step 1` DIVIDED BY 100) TIMES `step 2`
            WHEN `cost` THEN (`step 1` DIVIDED BY 100) TIMES `the service`'s `its cost, or the rules' amount for it`

-- s 273(3): "The registered provider must not require payment of the contribution before the funded aged care service is
-- delivered to the individual."
@export Can my provider make me pay my contribution yet (s 273(3))?
GIVEN `the service has been delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the service has been delivered to you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my provider make me pay my contribution yet` IF
    `the service has been delivered`

§§ `s 319 -- the daily means tested amount (residential care)`

-- s 319(1) Steps 1-7, the per day income tested amount: nothing up to "the total assessable income free area"; "50% of that
-- excess, divided by 364" up to the first income threshold; then flat to the second; "50% of the excess above the second income
-- threshold" up to the third; flat to the fourth; "50% of the excess above the fourth income threshold" beyond. Steps 8-14, the
-- per day asset tested amount, have the same shape at 17.5% (asset free area to first threshold) and 7.8% (second to third, and
-- above the fourth). "The daily means tested amount is the sum of the per day income tested amount and the per day asset tested
-- amount." s 319(2): the income free area is built from Social Security Act 1991 points 1064-B1, 1064-BA4 and 1064-E4; (4): all
-- eight thresholds "have the meaning prescribed by the rules". All are INPUTS.
DECLARE `The means test numbers`
    HAS `total assessable income free area` IS A NUMBER
        `first income threshold` IS A NUMBER
        `second income threshold` IS A NUMBER
        `third income threshold` IS A NUMBER
        `fourth income threshold` IS A NUMBER
        `asset free area` IS A NUMBER
        `first asset threshold` IS A NUMBER
        `second asset threshold` IS A NUMBER
        `third asset threshold` IS A NUMBER
        `fourth asset threshold` IS A NUMBER

-- The shared shape of Steps 2-7 and 9-14: rate1 above the free area to t1, rate2 above t2 to t3, rate2 above t4. Each step
-- names the whole band below it, so the bands simply add.
GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
      `free` IS A NUMBER
      `t1` IS A NUMBER
      `t2` IS A NUMBER
      `t3` IS A NUMBER
      `t4` IS A NUMBER
      `rate1` IS A NUMBER
      `rate2` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tested amount per day` MEANS
    (  `rate1` TIMES (`the greater of` 0 ((`the lesser of` `x` `t1`) MINUS `free`))
     PLUS `rate2` TIMES (`the greater of` 0 ((`the lesser of` `x` `t3`) MINUS `t2`))
     PLUS `rate2` TIMES (`the greater of` 0 (`x` MINUS `t4`)))
    DIVIDED BY 364

@export What is my per day income tested amount (s 319(1) Steps 1-7)?
GIVEN `my total assessable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total assessable income for a year, as determined under s 322
      `the numbers` IS A `The means test numbers` @desc The free areas and thresholds (Aged Care Rules; Social Security Act 1991 s 1064)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my per day income tested amount` MEANS
    `the tested amount per day` `my total assessable income`
        (`the numbers`'s `total assessable income free area`) (`the numbers`'s `first income threshold`)
        (`the numbers`'s `second income threshold`) (`the numbers`'s `third income threshold`) (`the numbers`'s `fourth income threshold`)
        0.5 0.5

@export What is my per day asset tested amount (s 319(1) Steps 8-14)?
GIVEN `the value of my assets` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of your assets, as determined under s 329
      `the numbers` IS A `The means test numbers` @desc The free areas and thresholds (Aged Care Rules)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my per day asset tested amount` MEANS
    `the tested amount per day` `the value of my assets`
        (`the numbers`'s `asset free area`) (`the numbers`'s `first asset threshold`)
        (`the numbers`'s `second asset threshold`) (`the numbers`'s `third asset threshold`) (`the numbers`'s `fourth asset threshold`)
        0.175 0.078

@export What is my daily means tested amount (s 319(1))?
GIVEN `my total assessable income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your total assessable income for a year, as determined under s 322
      `the value of my assets` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of your assets, as determined under s 329
      `the numbers` IS A `The means test numbers` @desc The free areas and thresholds
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my daily means tested amount` MEANS
    `What is my per day income tested amount` `my total assessable income` `the numbers`
        PLUS `What is my per day asset tested amount` `the value of my assets` `the numbers`

-- s 319(3): "The asset free area is: (a) unless paragraph (b) applies--the amount equal to 2.25 times the basic age pension
-- amount; or (b) if rules are in force for the purposes of this paragraph--such other amount as is calculated in accordance with
-- the rules." s 7: "basic age pension amount means the annual maximum basic rate under point 1064-B1 of the Social Security Act
-- 1991" for a person not a member of a couple.
@export What is my asset free area (s 319(3))?
GIVEN `the basic age pension amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The annual maximum basic rate of age pension for a single person (Social Security Act 1991 point 1064-B1)
      `rules set the asset free area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Aged Care Rules are in force for s 319(3)(b)
      `the rules' asset free area` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount those rules give, if any
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my asset free area` MEANS
    IF `rules set the asset free area` THEN `the rules' asset free area`
    ELSE 2.25 TIMES `the basic age pension amount`

§§ `ss 276-280 -- what I contribute in a residential care home each day`

-- s 277(2): "The basic daily fee for an individual is: (a) the amount prescribed by, or worked out in accordance with, the rules;
-- or (b) if no rules are in force for the purposes of paragraph (a)--the amount obtained by rounding down to the nearest cent the
-- amount equal to 85% of the basic age pension amount (worked out on a per day basis)." The Act does not say how the annual
-- amount is "worked out on a per day basis"; the per-day amount is an INPUT.
@export What is my basic daily fee (s 277(2))?
GIVEN `the basic age pension amount per day` IS A NUMBER @desc The single basic age pension amount, worked out on a per day basis
      `rules set the basic daily fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Aged Care Rules are in force for s 277(2)(a)
      `the rules' basic daily fee` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount those rules give, if any
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my basic daily fee` MEANS
    IF `rules set the basic daily fee` THEN `the rules' basic daily fee`
    ELSE `rounded down to the cent` (0.85 TIMES `the basic age pension amount per day`)

-- s 278(1): "Step 2. If the individual's daily means tested amount exceeds the maximum accommodation supplement amount ..., the
-- hotelling contribution is the lesser of: (a) the daily means tested amount minus the maximum accommodation supplement amount;
-- and (b) the maximum hotelling supplement amount ... Step 3. If the individual's daily means tested amount does not exceed the
-- maximum accommodation supplement amount, the hotelling contribution is zero." (2): with means not disclosed status, "the
-- maximum hotelling supplement amount". s 280(1): taken to be zero while a hardship determination under s 280(2) is in force or
-- the individual is in a class prescribed by the rules. Gloss: s 235(3), (4) make both maxima "the highest of the amounts
-- prescribed by the rules" (INPUTS).
DECLARE `My residential means`
    HAS `my daily means tested amount` IS A NUMBER
        `I have means not disclosed status` IS A BOOLEAN
        `the maximum accommodation supplement amount` IS A NUMBER
        `the maximum hotelling supplement amount` IS A NUMBER
        `the maximum non-clinical care contribution` IS A NUMBER
        `my contributions are taken to be zero under s 280` IS A BOOLEAN

@export What is my hotelling contribution for a day (ss 278, 280)?
GIVEN `my means` IS A `My residential means` @desc Your daily means tested amount and the rules' maxima for the day
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my hotelling contribution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `my means`'s `my contributions are taken to be zero under s 280` THEN 0
        IF `my means`'s `I have means not disclosed status` THEN `my means`'s `the maximum hotelling supplement amount`
        IF `my means`'s `my daily means tested amount` GREATER THAN `my means`'s `the maximum accommodation supplement amount`
           THEN `the lesser of` (`my means`'s `my daily means tested amount` MINUS `my means`'s `the maximum accommodation supplement amount`)
                                (`my means`'s `the maximum hotelling supplement amount`)
        OTHERWISE 0

-- s 279(1): "Step 2. Work out the sum of: (a) the maximum accommodation supplement amount ...; and (b) the maximum hotelling
-- supplement amount ... Step 3. If the individual's daily means tested amount exceeds the result of Step 2, the non-clinical care
-- contribution is the lesser of: (a) the daily means tested amount minus the result of Step 2; and (b) the maximum non-clinical
-- care contribution". (2): with means not disclosed status, "the maximum non-clinical care contribution". (4): zero once there
-- have been "the number of days prescribed by the rules" on which it could have been charged. (5): zero once the lifetime cap is
-- passed. s 280(1): zero under a hardship determination.
@export What is my non-clinical care contribution for a day (ss 279, 280)?
GIVEN `my means` IS A `My residential means` @desc Your daily means tested amount and the rules' maxima for the day
      `the rules' number of chargeable days has been reached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the days on which it could have been charged have reached the number prescribed by the rules (s 279(4))
      `the lifetime cap has been passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, on an earlier day, your counted contributions exceeded the lifetime cap (s 279(5))
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my non-clinical care contribution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `my means`'s `my contributions are taken to be zero under s 280`
           OR `the rules' number of chargeable days has been reached`
           OR `the lifetime cap has been passed`
           THEN 0
        IF `my means`'s `I have means not disclosed status` THEN `my means`'s `the maximum non-clinical care contribution`
        IF `my means`'s `my daily means tested amount` GREATER THAN `step 2`
           THEN `the lesser of` (`my means`'s `my daily means tested amount` MINUS `step 2`) (`my means`'s `the maximum non-clinical care contribution`)
        OTHERWISE 0
    WHERE
        `step 2` MEANS `my means`'s `the maximum accommodation supplement amount` PLUS `my means`'s `the maximum hotelling supplement amount`

-- s 277(1): "Step 1. Work out the basic daily fee ... Step 2. Add the compensation payment fee (if any) ... Step 3. Add the
-- hotelling contribution (if any) ... Step 4. Add the non-clinical care contribution (if any)". s 276(2)(a): the resident
-- contribution "must not exceed the sum of: (a) the maximum daily amount of the resident contribution worked out for the day under
-- section 277; and (b) such other amounts as are prescribed by ... the rules". The s 277(4) reductions and the s 276(2)(b) amounts
-- are not encoded; the compensation payment fee is an INPUT (s 277(3)).
@export What is the most my resident contribution can be for a day (ss 276(2)(a), 277(1))?
GIVEN `my basic daily fee` IS A NUMBER @desc Your basic daily fee (s 277(2))
      `my compensation payment fee` IS A NUMBER @desc Your compensation payment fee for the day, if any (s 277(3))
      `my means` IS A `My residential means` @desc Your daily means tested amount and the rules' maxima for the day
      `the rules' number of chargeable days has been reached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the s 279(4) number of days has been reached
      `the lifetime cap has been passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the lifetime cap has been passed (s 279(5))
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most my resident contribution can be for a day` MEANS
    `my basic daily fee`
        PLUS `my compensation payment fee`
        PLUS `What is my hotelling contribution` `my means`
        PLUS `What is my non-clinical care contribution` `my means` `the rules' number of chargeable days has been reached` `the lifetime cap has been passed`

-- s 281(3): "The period (the pre-entry period) is the period: (a) starting on the later of the following: (i) the day the
-- individual enters into a service agreement with the provider; (ii) the day that is 7 days before the individual's start day;
-- and (b) ending at the end of the day before that start day." (4)(b): at most 85% of the basic age pension amount per day,
-- rounded down to the cent, if no rules are in force.
@export On how many days before I move in can I be charged a pre-entry fee (s 281(3))?
GIVEN `days between my service agreement and my start day` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days before your start day you entered into the service agreement
GIVETH A NUMBER
`On how many days can I be charged a pre-entry fee` MEANS
    `the greater of` 0 (`the lesser of` `days between my service agreement and my start day` 7)

-- s 282(2): a bed reservation fee may be charged for a day if the individual "(a) is absent from the approved residential care
-- home on the day; and (b) is not on leave ... (see section 244); and (c) would have been on social leave ... except that the
-- individual has previously been on social leave during the current financial year for 52 days." s 244(7)(c): social leave only
-- while previous social leave days in the financial year are "less than 52".
@export May I be charged a bed reservation fee for a day away (ss 244(7), 282(2))?
GIVEN `I am away from the home the whole day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are absent from the home for the whole day
      `I am on emergency, hospital or hospital transition leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are on another kind of leave that day (s 244(3)-(6))
      `social leave days already taken this financial year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days of social leave you have already had this financial year
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be charged a bed reservation fee` IF
        `I am away from the home the whole day`
    AND (NOT `I am on emergency, hospital or hospital transition leave`)
    AND `social leave days already taken this financial year` AT LEAST 52

§§ `ss 296, 298, 301, 305 -- paying for my room`

-- s 296(a): "the individual must not be charged an accommodation payment unless: (i) the individual's daily means tested amount,
-- at the individual's start day, is equal to or greater than the individual's maximum accommodation supplement amount for that
-- day; or (ii) the individual has means not disclosed status at the individual's start day; or (iii) at the individual's start
-- day, the individual's daily means tested amount has not been determined and the individual does not have means not disclosed
-- status". s 298(a): "an individual must not be charged an accommodation contribution unless the individual's daily means tested
-- amount, at the individual's start day, is less than the maximum accommodation supplement amount for that day". Gloss: an
-- accommodation payment is the room price agreed with the home (s 294); an accommodation contribution is the lower, means-tested
-- amount.
DECLARE `What I can be charged for my room` IS ONE OF
    `an accommodation payment`
    `an accommodation contribution`

@export Can I be charged an accommodation payment or only an accommodation contribution (ss 296(a), 298(a))?
GIVEN `my daily means tested amount has been determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your daily means tested amount had been determined at your start day
      `my daily means tested amount at my start day` IS A NUMBER @desc Your daily means tested amount at your start day
      `the maximum accommodation supplement amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum accommodation supplement amount for your start day (s 235(3))
      `I have means not disclosed status` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had means not disclosed status at your start day
GIVETH A `What I can be charged for my room`
`What can I be charged for my room` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `I have means not disclosed status` OR (NOT `my daily means tested amount has been determined`) THEN `an accommodation payment`
        IF `my daily means tested amount at my start day` AT LEAST `the maximum accommodation supplement amount` THEN `an accommodation payment`
        OTHERWISE `an accommodation contribution`

-- s 298(b): "the amount of daily accommodation contribution for a day must not exceed: (i) the maximum accommodation supplement
-- amount for that day; or (ii) the amount assessed for the individual based on the individual's daily means tested amount"; (c):
-- unless the rules provide otherwise, not "greater than the agreed accommodation payment amount ... (as expressed as a daily
-- accommodation payment amount ...)". INFERENCE: "must not exceed (i) ... or (ii)" is read as must exceed neither, so the cap is
-- the least of the three. The amount assessed on the means is worked out under rules not deposited (an INPUT).
@export What is the most my daily accommodation contribution can be (s 298(b), (c))?
GIVEN `the maximum accommodation supplement amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum accommodation supplement amount for the day
      `the amount assessed on my means` IS A NUMBER @desc The daily amount assessed for you on your daily means tested amount
      `my agreed accommodation payment as a daily amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The agreed accommodation payment amount for you and the home, as a daily amount
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most my daily accommodation contribution can be` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`the lesser of` `the maximum accommodation supplement amount` `the amount assessed on my means`)
                    `my agreed accommodation payment as a daily amount`

-- s 301: interest may be charged on a daily payment that "(a) is payable by the individual; and (b) has been outstanding for more
-- than one month"; (2) only if "the individual's accommodation agreement provides for the charging of such interest at a specified
-- rate"; (3) "the rate charged must not exceed the maximum rate prescribed by the rules".
@export May I be charged interest on an overdue daily payment (s 301)?
GIVEN `it has been outstanding for more than a month` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the daily payment has been outstanding for more than one month
      `my accommodation agreement provides for interest at a specified rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your accommodation agreement provides for interest at a specified rate
      `the rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The interest rate charged
      `the rules' maximum rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum rate prescribed by the Aged Care Rules
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be charged interest on an overdue daily payment` IF
        `it has been outstanding for more than a month`
    AND `my accommodation agreement provides for interest at a specified rate`
    AND `the rate` AT MOST `the rules' maximum rate`

-- s 305(2): "The minimum permissible asset value is: (a) the amount obtained by rounding to the nearest $500.00 (rounding $250.00
-- upwards) the amount equal to 2.25 times the basic age pension amount at the time the registered provider starts delivering
-- ongoing funded aged care services to the individual in an approved residential care home; or (b) such higher amount as is
-- prescribed by the rules."
@export What is the least I must be left with if I pay a refundable deposit (s 305(2))?
GIVEN `the basic age pension amount` IS A NUMBER @desc The annual single basic age pension amount when your residential care started
      `a higher amount the rules prescribe` IS A NUMBER @desc A higher amount prescribed by the Aged Care Rules, or 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my minimum permissible asset value` MEANS
    `the greater of` `rounded` `a higher amount the rules prescribe`
    WHERE
        `rounded` MEANS 500 TIMES (TRUNC (((2.25 TIMES `the basic age pension amount`) PLUS 250) DIVIDED BY 500) 0)

-- s 305(1): "A registered provider must not accept payment of an amount of refundable deposit from an individual if: (a) the
-- individual provides sufficient information to allow the individual's daily means tested amount to be worked out; and (b) the
-- individual pays the amount within 28 days after the individual's start day; and (c) payment of the amount would leave the value
-- of the individual's remaining assets at less than the minimum permissible asset value."
@export May my provider accept this refundable deposit from me (s 305(1))?
GIVEN `I gave enough information to work out my daily means tested amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you provided enough information for your daily means tested amount to be worked out
      `days after my start day I pay` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after your start day you pay the amount
      `my assets left after paying` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of your remaining assets after the payment (worked out as under s 330, disregarding s 330(7))
      `my minimum permissible asset value` IS A NUMBER @desc Your minimum permissible asset value (s 305(2))
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my provider accept this refundable deposit` IF
    NOT (    `I gave enough information to work out my daily means tested amount`
         AND `days after my start day I pay` AT MOST 28
         AND `my assets left after paying` LESS THAN `my minimum permissible asset value`)

§§ `ss 23, 24, 358 -- the Statement of Rights`

-- s 23 sets out the Statement of Rights in thirteen subsections. Each value below names one, in the Act's order.
DECLARE `A right I may ask about` IS ONE OF
    `to make my own choices about my services, my finances and my possessions, with support if needed`
    `to equitable access to assessment, and to palliative and end-of-life care`
    `to dignity, respect, fair treatment and culturally safe services from qualified workers`
    `to be free from violence, abuse, neglect, exploitation and coercion`
    `to privacy and protection of my personal information`
    `to records and information about my rights, my services and their costs`
    `to be informed about my services in a way I understand, and to be heard`
    `to communicate in my preferred language, with interpreters and aids`
    `to complain without fear of reprisal and have it dealt with fairly and promptly`
    `to be supported by an advocate or other person of my choice`
    `to have the role of my carers, visitors and volunteers respected`
    `to stay connected with family, friends, pets, community and Country`
    `to access at any time a person I designate`
    `to choose among services I have not been approved to access`

-- s 23(1)(a): choice "including in relation to ... (i) the funded aged care services the individual has been approved to access";
-- (2)-(13) as glossed in the values above. Nothing in s 23 gives a right to services beyond the approval.
@export Does the Statement of Rights give me this right (s 23)?
GIVEN `the right` IS A `A right I may ask about` @desc The right you ask about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Statement of Rights give me this right` IF
    CONSIDER `the right`
    WHEN `to choose among services I have not been approved to access` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 24(1): "An individual is entitled to the rights specified in section 23 when accessing, or seeking to access, funded aged
-- care services."
@export Am I entitled to the Statement of Rights (s 24(1))?
GIVEN `I am accessing or seeking to access funded aged care services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are accessing, or seeking to access, funded aged care services
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to the Statement of Rights` IF
    `I am accessing or seeking to access funded aged care services`

-- s 24(3): "Nothing in this Division creates rights or duties that are enforceable by proceedings in a court or tribunal." Note
-- to s 24: "A person may make a complaint to the Complaints Commissioner about a registered provider acting in a way that is
-- incompatible with the Statement of Rights: see section 358." s 358(a)(ii): the Complaints Commissioner maintains processes for
-- "making complaints about a registered provider acting in a way that is incompatible with the Statement of Rights".
DECLARE `Where I can take a breach of my rights` IS ONE OF
    `the Complaints Commissioner`
    `nowhere under this Act`

@export Where can I take a provider that is not respecting my Statement of Rights (ss 24(3), 358(a)(ii))?
GIVEN `I am accessing or seeking to access funded aged care services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are accessing, or seeking to access, funded aged care services
GIVETH A `Where I can take a breach of my rights`
`Where can I take a breach of my rights` MEANS
    IF `I am accessing or seeking to access funded aged care services`
    THEN `the Complaints Commissioner`
    ELSE `nowhere under this Act`

@export Can I sue in a court or tribunal to enforce my Statement of Rights (s 24(3))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I sue to enforce my Statement of Rights` IF FALSE
